/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  ctrl14_williams_otto_pi  --  the paper's setpoint-tracking experiment
                               (section 4.2, Figure 4), reproduced.

  The control channel (F_fB, F_pP) of eq. (4.6) with the paper's own
  Skogestad-IMC tunings drives the product stream from its nominal
  3.90 klb/h to the setpoint 4.5 klb/h.  Figure 4's shape: F_fB overshoots
  to ~23 klb/h around 10 h after activation, backs off, settles ~21;
  F_pP overshoots to ~4.6 and settles onto 4.5 by ~40 h.

  The paper activates its PI at t* = 100 h with the plant already settled;
  here the plant STARTS at the settled state (ctrl12's converged x*,
  machine-accurate) with the PI on from t = 0 -- the same experiment with
  the flat prefix removed, which is exactly the segment the figure plots.

  Gain conversion, stated once: K3prop = 0.069 is a klb/h-per-klb/h ratio
  and survives the SI boundary unchanged; K3int = 1.282 per hour becomes
  3.5611e-4 per second.  The golden pins the settled F_pP on the setpoint
  and F_fB on its Fig. 4 plateau.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

application   choupoCtrl;
description   "Williams-Otto PI channel (F_fB, F_pP), paper eq. 4.6 with the section-4.1 tunings: F_pP tracks 3.90 -> 4.5 klb/h with the Fig. 4 overshoot";

verbosity     3;

startTime       0;         // s
endTime         360000;    // s  (100 h -- Fig. 4's window after activation)
deltaT          60;        // s
writeInterval   7200;      // s  (2 h -> 50 frames, the transient visible)
